what is the reparemetrization invariance of $$\tag{0.1}
\begin{align}
S & =-m\int \mathrm{d}\tau \sqrt{ -g_{\mu \nu} \frac{\mathrm{d} x^{\mu}}{\mathrm{d} \tau} \frac{\mathrm{d} x^{\nu}}{\mathrm{d} \tau} }+q\int \mathrm{d}\tau A_{\mu} \frac{\mathrm{d}x^{\mu}}{\mathrm{d}\tau}
\end{align}
$$
? what is the corresponding Noether charge? view $x^{\mu}$ as world line field.

the action of a particle with background gravitational and electric fields is

$$\tag{1.1}
\begin{align}
S_{p} & =-m\int \mathrm{d}\tau \sqrt{ -g_{\mu \nu} \frac{\mathrm{d}x^{\mu}}{\mathrm{d}\tau} \frac{\mathrm{d}x^{\nu}}{\mathrm{d}\tau} }+q\int \mathrm{d}\tau A_{\mu} \frac{\mathrm{d}x^{\mu}}{\mathrm{d}\tau}
\end{align}
$$

consider the infinitesimal diffeomorphism generated by $\displaystyle{\xi ^{\mu}}$

$$\tag{1.2}
\begin{align}
0 =\delta _{\xi}S_{p} & =\int \mathrm{d}^{4}x\sqrt{ -g }\nabla _{\mu}[T^{\mu \nu}\xi _{\nu}+j^{\mu}A^{\nu}\xi _{\nu}]-\int \mathrm{d}\tau  \frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}\tau}\left((mU_{\nu}+qA_{\nu})\xi ^{\nu}\right)+(\text{ bulk terms })
\end{align}
$$

where $\displaystyle{U^{\mu}= \frac{\mathrm{d}x^{\mu}}{\mathrm{d}\tau}}$ and $\displaystyle{T^{\mu \nu}, j ^{\mu}}$ are defined as

$$\tag{1.3}
\begin{align}
T^{\mu \nu} & = m\int \mathrm{d}\tau U^{\mu}U^{\nu} \frac{\delta ^{4}(x-x(\tau))}{\sqrt{ -g }} \\
j ^{\mu} & =q\int \mathrm{d}\tau U^{\mu} \frac{\delta ^{4}(x-x(\tau))}{\sqrt{ -g }}
\end{align}
$$

how can be states that $\displaystyle{\int \mathrm{d}^{4}x\sqrt{ -g }\nabla _{\mu}[T^{\mu \nu}\xi _{\nu}+j^{\mu}A^{\nu}\xi _{\nu}]-\int \mathrm{d}\tau  \frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}\tau}\left((mU_{\nu}+qA_{\nu})\xi ^{\nu}\right)}$ by direct calculation?

use covariant phase space formalism discuss the following action
S & =\frac{1}{16\pi G}\int _{M}\varepsilon R-\frac{1}{4\pi}\int _{M}\varepsilon F_{\mu \nu}F^{\mu \nu}
derive the 1st law of black hole thermodynamics for Kerr-Newman black hole.
